WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:01.834
-Welcome back, everybody.

00:00:01.834 --> 00:00:03.534
We're hanging out
with John Legend.

00:00:03.534 --> 00:00:06.100
-Hello.

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:09.868
-We have a lot to talk about,
the album, "Legend."

00:00:09.868 --> 00:00:11.100
We have to talk about
"The Voice."

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:13.300
-It was nice though taking
a trip down memory lane.

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:15.100
-Yeah, I remember that band.

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:16.367
-Our group was special.

00:00:16.367 --> 00:00:18.133
-It was something.
It was tight, yeah.

00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:19.968
How is Chrissy doing?
How is the family?

00:00:19.968 --> 00:00:22.067
-Everybody's good.
-Please give them my best.

00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:24.901
-We're having a baby sometime
in the next few months.

00:00:24.901 --> 00:00:26.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.067
-Congratulations.
That's so good.

00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:30.534
-The kids are very excited.
They're back at school now.

00:00:30.534 --> 00:00:33.033
-It's all happening.
-Luna's in first grade now.

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.968
Crazy. Crazy.
-It happens so fast, buddy.

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:38.234
-I know Chrissy is the chef in
the family, okay but, you --

00:00:38.234 --> 00:00:40.701
-I can cook though. I can cook.

00:00:40.701 --> 00:00:42.667
I can throw down.
-I know.

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:46.334
Well, there's a thing that you
started a little controversy.

00:00:46.334 --> 00:00:47.734
-Controversy
as the Brits would say.

00:00:47.734 --> 00:00:51.467
-Yes, of course, on the Internet
and on Instagram.

00:00:51.467 --> 00:00:55.234
A little controversy
because you said that

00:00:55.234 --> 00:01:00.367
chicken and waffles are good but
chicken and pancakes are better.

00:01:00.367 --> 00:01:02.501
-I stand by it. I stand by it.

00:01:02.501 --> 00:01:04.167
Y'all doubting it
because y'all haven't tried it.

00:01:04.167 --> 00:01:05.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.634 --> 00:01:07.267
-"Chicken and pancakes are
greater than

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:09.234
chicken and waffles, fight me,"
is what you put.

00:01:09.234 --> 00:01:10.501
-I did. I did.

00:01:10.501 --> 00:01:11.567
-Yeah, that's hilarious.

00:01:11.567 --> 00:01:13.467
-That's how we say it
on the Internet.

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:15.367
-But what kind of reaction
did this get?

00:01:15.367 --> 00:01:18.200
-I got some agreement,
some skepticism.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:20.467
But I know I'm right,
so, you know?

00:01:20.467 --> 00:01:21.367
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:23.200
-Well, I don't know.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:24.968
I would say chicken and waffles.

00:01:24.968 --> 00:01:26.734
-Have you ever tried
chicken and pancakes?

00:01:26.734 --> 00:01:28.767
-I've never.
-Bubby's has some in New York.

00:01:28.767 --> 00:01:30.601
You should try that.
-This is from Bubby's.

00:01:30.601 --> 00:01:32.167
-Oh, this is from Bubby's.

00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:35.334
-We actually --
We heard that you like Bubby's.

00:01:35.334 --> 00:01:38.434
But why pancakes over waffles?

00:01:38.434 --> 00:01:40.934
-I think it's a texture thing
because they're basically made

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:43.167
with the same batter --
similar batter.

00:01:43.167 --> 00:01:46.601
But I like the soft, fluffy
texture of a pancake

00:01:46.601 --> 00:01:47.901
with the crispy chicken.

00:01:47.901 --> 00:01:49.801
I think it goes well.

00:01:49.801 --> 00:01:54.100
I like the combination of the
soft and the crispy together.

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:55.834
I think it's better.

00:01:55.834 --> 00:01:58.834
I'm sure Ahmir has thoughts
on this.

00:01:58.834 --> 00:02:00.934
-Actually, we agree.

00:02:00.934 --> 00:02:03.367
-Okay, alright.
-Tariq too?

00:02:03.367 --> 00:02:05.801
-Yeah, there's a Bubby's
in LaGuardia,

00:02:05.801 --> 00:02:06.834
like, in the new terminal

00:02:06.834 --> 00:02:09.400
and they have the pancakes and
chicken.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:12.834
-Hey, I didn't know you were
a spokesperson for Bubby's.

00:02:12.834 --> 00:02:16.801
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.801 --> 00:02:19.634
Don't name all the locations.
Here we go.

00:02:19.634 --> 00:02:21.701
Do you think -- You agree?

00:02:21.701 --> 00:02:23.701
-Yes.
-Yeah.

00:02:23.701 --> 00:02:25.367
-I'm going to try this right now
because I do not agree.

00:02:25.367 --> 00:02:27.000
I think you want
that little crunch.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:30.167
-A little crunch
and a little fluffy.

00:02:30.167 --> 00:02:32.267
-I'm going to do --
I'm doing a little syrup too.

00:02:32.267 --> 00:02:34.734
-Mmm-mmm-mmm.
That's good chicken too.

00:02:34.734 --> 00:02:36.534
-Wait, I can't even
slice the pancake.

00:02:36.534 --> 00:02:38.467
Alright, here we go.

00:02:38.467 --> 00:02:41.267
Alright.
-I make a mean pancake myself.

00:02:41.267 --> 00:02:43.601
That's our Sunday tradition
at our house.

00:02:43.601 --> 00:02:45.367
I make pancakes every Sunday.

00:02:45.367 --> 00:02:47.434
-That pancake's good.
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:53.234
It's a blessing.
That's delicious.

00:02:53.234 --> 00:02:55.767
-He's right.
That's unbelievable.

00:02:55.767 --> 00:02:57.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:57.334 --> 00:02:59.100
It's actually better
than waffles.

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:01.834
This is a big thing.

00:03:01.834 --> 00:03:04.234
Dude, this is a big --
This is a giant thing.

00:03:04.234 --> 00:03:05.634
I've never done this.

00:03:05.634 --> 00:03:07.367
-And now that
your eyes are open,

00:03:07.367 --> 00:03:09.868
you can't see the world
any differently now.

00:03:09.868 --> 00:03:12.000
-I feel like a new man.
-You're a new man.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.300
-Yeah.
-You've been converted.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:15.100
Welcome, welcome.
-Wow, I'm so happy!

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:17.701
Chicken and pancakes, who knew?

00:03:17.701 --> 00:03:19.634
Chicken and pancakes.

00:03:19.634 --> 00:03:23.100
And Bubby's, there's like six
locations in the city, Tariq.

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:24.300
There's one --

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:27.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.601 --> 00:03:30.634
-Tariq has a sponsored post
on Instagram.

00:03:30.634 --> 00:03:32.467
-Bubby's.

00:03:32.467 --> 00:03:35.100
I love following you
on all the socials.

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:36.634
You do have a strong opinion
about stuff.

00:03:36.634 --> 00:03:39.434
But I do also like
obviously your music.

00:03:39.434 --> 00:03:42.767
You do funny things
but also your activism.

00:03:42.767 --> 00:03:44.767
And a lot of people
on the Internet have said

00:03:44.767 --> 00:03:46.534
they want you maybe
to run for office.

00:03:46.534 --> 00:03:48.033
-No.

00:03:48.033 --> 00:03:51.033
-Not even thinking about it?
Not even thinking about it?

00:03:51.033 --> 00:03:52.234
-Not even thinking about it.

00:03:52.234 --> 00:03:55.834
I truly enjoy what I do
and I enjoy my life.

00:03:55.834 --> 00:03:57.634
And I do not want to run
for office.

00:03:57.634 --> 00:03:59.934
It doesn't seem fun to me.

00:03:59.934 --> 00:04:04.300
-It doesn't. I looked on
the inner-webs to see about

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:07.667
this theory, and I found out
that this John Legend actually

00:04:07.667 --> 00:04:10.501
did run for office
and win in high school.

00:04:10.501 --> 00:04:12.667
-I ran for student body
president.

00:04:12.667 --> 00:04:14.334
[ Audience aws ]

00:04:14.334 --> 00:04:16.801
I was the student body president
at my high school in Ohio.

00:04:16.801 --> 00:04:18.200
-You were?
-Yeah.

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:21.334
-And what did you accomplish
there as student body president?

00:04:21.334 --> 00:04:24.000
-Well, we had to plan a lot of
events and different things.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:27.367
We had a lot of meetings. I
started a peer tutoring program.

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:28.601
-Did you really?
-Yeah.

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:30.868
-That's fantastic.
-Yeah.

00:04:30.868 --> 00:04:33.701
-Do you remember your campaign?
Do you remember what you ran on?

00:04:33.701 --> 00:04:36.734
-Well, I gave a speech and then
at the end, I sang a little bit.

00:04:36.734 --> 00:04:38.334
-You had to.
-'Cause why not? Why not?

00:04:38.334 --> 00:04:41.634
-You had to sing.
-I just sang at the end of it.

00:04:41.634 --> 00:04:44.734
Just put a button on it at
the end, and "vote for me."

00:04:44.734 --> 00:04:46.901
My brother actually cut my hair.

00:04:46.901 --> 00:04:49.467
You met him backstage.
He cuts my hair still.

00:04:49.467 --> 00:04:53.033
But back then he put
"J.R.S. for Pres" in my hair.

00:04:53.033 --> 00:04:54.501
John Roger Stephens,
that's my real name.

00:04:54.501 --> 00:04:56.133
-Dude, that's a slam dunk.

00:04:56.133 --> 00:04:57.834
That's like, come on.
-That's all it took.

00:04:57.834 --> 00:04:59.267
-Well, let's talk about --
I want to talk about "Legend."

00:04:59.267 --> 00:05:00.667
Let's talk about this.
Here we go.

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:03.667
It is out today. It's out.
-It's out.

00:05:03.667 --> 00:05:05.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:05.334 --> 00:05:07.400
-Can I just say, too,

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:09.968
it's hard enough to just release
one album.

00:05:09.968 --> 00:05:11.834
But this is technically
two albums.

00:05:11.834 --> 00:05:14.367
-Yeah, it's a double album.
There's 12 songs on each side.

00:05:14.367 --> 00:05:15.701
I had a lot of time, though.

00:05:15.701 --> 00:05:17.534
We couldn't go on tour
for a long time.

00:05:17.534 --> 00:05:18.701
-24 songs?

00:05:18.701 --> 00:05:20.434
-And this is what the pandemic
has brought.

00:05:20.434 --> 00:05:22.934
I made more songs than I'm
usually used to making

00:05:22.934 --> 00:05:24.834
for an album so I figured
let's make it a double album.

00:05:24.834 --> 00:05:26.367
-Did you think about
spacing it out

00:05:26.367 --> 00:05:27.734
and going like,
"I'll put one out now

00:05:27.734 --> 00:05:30.334
and I'll take a year off"?
-No, because by the time I would

00:05:30.334 --> 00:05:32.067
put it out, the second one,

00:05:32.067 --> 00:05:34.033
I'd be already writing
new stuff,

00:05:34.033 --> 00:05:36.033
and I would feel weird about
putting out old stuff.

00:05:36.033 --> 00:05:37.634
So I was just like,
"Let's just put it all out."

00:05:37.634 --> 00:05:39.133
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:05:39.133 --> 00:05:42.767
-You went on the Internet and
announced the title, "Legend."

00:05:42.767 --> 00:05:45.801
And Chrissy, your wife,
commented,

00:05:45.801 --> 00:05:48.534
"Love to find out the album name
with everyone else.

00:05:48.534 --> 00:05:51.868
Keeping me humble."
-See, I dispute that contention.

00:05:51.868 --> 00:05:55.167
I told her when I was --
I was literally showing her

00:05:55.167 --> 00:05:57.501
different versions
of the album cover.

00:05:57.501 --> 00:05:59.067
And I told her the album was
called "Legend"

00:05:59.067 --> 00:06:00.534
and then I reminded her of that.

00:06:00.534 --> 00:06:02.167
She's like, "Oh, yeah, you're
probably right. I forgot."

00:06:02.167 --> 00:06:03.434
[ Laughter ]

00:06:03.434 --> 00:06:05.634
-That's a good impression of
Chrissy, by the way.

00:06:05.634 --> 00:06:07.701
"Oh, yeah, you're right.
I probably forgot."

00:06:07.701 --> 00:06:09.601
But there's some great
collaborations.

00:06:09.601 --> 00:06:11.367
-Yes. We got Jazmine Sullivan.

00:06:11.367 --> 00:06:13.567
-Ty Dolla $ign.
-Ty Dolla $ign.

00:06:13.567 --> 00:06:15.267
Jhene Aiko. Rapsody.
-Saweetie.

00:06:15.267 --> 00:06:18.567
-Saweetie. Rick Ross.
-Rick Ross.

00:06:18.567 --> 00:06:20.334
-Ledisi.

00:06:20.334 --> 00:06:23.834
-And the music video you did
with Saweetie was really fun.

00:06:23.834 --> 00:06:26.100
-It was very cool.
So we shot it in Miami.

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:30.868
And the director's idea was to
basically allow our dancers

00:06:30.868 --> 00:06:32.968
to kind of freestyle
and be themselves.

00:06:32.968 --> 00:06:35.801
And so the idea was
that we told them

00:06:35.801 --> 00:06:37.934
this was the callback
for their audition.

00:06:37.934 --> 00:06:39.901
And they were just out there
freestyling.

00:06:39.901 --> 00:06:41.200
But we were filming it.

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:43.300
And then halfway through
the song, me and Saweetie

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:45.801
would surprise them
while they were dancing.

00:06:45.801 --> 00:06:48.701
And we got, like, genuine,
authentic reactions from them.

00:06:48.701 --> 00:06:50.934
It was amazing.
-It makes you just smile.

00:06:50.934 --> 00:06:52.501
It makes you go,
"Oh, this is so fun."

00:06:52.501 --> 00:06:54.701
-Yeah, they really loved it.
We loved it.

00:06:54.701 --> 00:06:56.667
It was really heartwarming,
and we had a good time.

00:06:56.667 --> 00:06:58.467
-Yeah, that's what we want.

00:06:58.467 --> 00:07:00.167
Can we talk about "The Voice"?
-Yes.

00:07:00.167 --> 00:07:03.934
-Season 22, September 19th
on NBC.

00:07:03.934 --> 00:07:06.400
-I'm in it to win it.

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:07.734
-Camila Cabello, though.

00:07:07.734 --> 00:07:10.267
-Camila Cabello
is our newest coach.

00:07:10.267 --> 00:07:11.734
-And she's a friend of the show.

00:07:11.734 --> 00:07:14.033
I know her.
I know she knows music.

00:07:14.033 --> 00:07:16.133
-She's very smart.
She's very competitive.

00:07:16.133 --> 00:07:20.133
I brought her on my team last
season to be my guest mentor,

00:07:20.133 --> 00:07:23.334
and it's like
I sabotaged myself.

00:07:23.334 --> 00:07:25.501
-You created a monster.
-I created a monster because

00:07:25.501 --> 00:07:28.300
she's coming back
with a lot of mojo,

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:29.501
a lot of competitive fire.

00:07:29.501 --> 00:07:31.267
-Didn't she get her start --

00:07:31.267 --> 00:07:33.434
-She was on "X Factor."
-"X Factor."

00:07:33.434 --> 00:07:36.434
-She was in that group
called Fifth Harmony.

00:07:36.434 --> 00:07:39.701
And they were assembled on
"X Factor,"

00:07:39.701 --> 00:07:41.234
just like One Direction was.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:41.234 --> 00:07:44.100
-So, she knows exactly how to --

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:45.868
Just even mentioning
One Direction, they go,

00:07:45.868 --> 00:07:47.567
"Oh, my God!"
They're not coming out.

00:07:47.567 --> 00:07:49.000
-Yes, but Simon, sometimes,

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:50.133
he knows how to put the groups
together.

00:07:50.133 --> 00:07:51.901
-He's smart, yeah.

00:07:51.901 --> 00:07:53.934
But she's lived through it,
so I think people probably

00:07:53.934 --> 00:07:56.801
look to her and go like, "Oh,
you know, that might be the --"

00:07:56.801 --> 00:07:58.367
-Quit making the pitch for her.

00:07:58.367 --> 00:08:00.200
Make her make her pitch
for herself.

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:02.701
I got to beat this girl.
-I know.

00:08:02.701 --> 00:08:05.300
Do you like when people
sing your songs?

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:07.133
Do you turn the chair
around and go --

00:08:07.133 --> 00:08:10.000
-I am particularly tough on
people when they sing my song.

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:12.334
And I think
it's a weakness of mine.

00:08:12.334 --> 00:08:14.367
It's my issue.
-'Cause why?

00:08:14.367 --> 00:08:16.567
-I nitpick it too much
when they sing my song.

00:08:16.567 --> 00:08:18.334
-So you're like --
Or do you go like,

00:08:18.334 --> 00:08:19.667
"Oh, I could have sung it
like that"?

00:08:19.667 --> 00:08:23.434
-Yeah. I had one guy that sang
my song "Glory,"

00:08:23.434 --> 00:08:25.834
and he did such a beautiful job.

00:08:25.834 --> 00:08:28.868
And he did new things to it
that I really loved,

00:08:28.868 --> 00:08:30.434
and I was like --
I turned for him.

00:08:30.434 --> 00:08:32.434
And he ended up going all
the way to the finals with me.

00:08:32.434 --> 00:08:34.834
His name was Victor.
-How about this year?

00:08:34.834 --> 00:08:37.234
You feeling good about it?
-I love my team this year.

00:08:37.234 --> 00:08:39.067
We're good. I feel like we're
going to win this year.

00:08:39.067 --> 00:08:40.901
-Alright, John Legend.
You heard it here first.

00:08:40.901 --> 00:08:43.300
-It's going to happen.
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:46.100
Here's a sneak peek at the new
season of "The Voice."

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:47.434
Take a look at this.

00:08:47.434 --> 00:08:50.200
-I turned for you first,
I would like to remind you.

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:52.167
It's obvious
that your voice is powerful.

00:08:52.167 --> 00:08:53.734
You have crazy range

00:08:53.734 --> 00:08:56.200
that most male singers
could never pull off.

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:59.100
There was something interesting
about the little turns

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:01.701
in your voice that were
very soulful to me.

00:09:01.701 --> 00:09:05.167
It sounded like a church singer
singing rock music sometimes.

00:09:05.167 --> 00:09:06.634
Honestly.
-That's exactly what I am.

00:09:06.634 --> 00:09:08.434
-Exactly.
-Grew up in church singing.

00:09:08.434 --> 00:09:10.400
-Okay, we're screwed.
-I heard that then.

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:11.734
That's why I was so floored
by you.

00:09:11.734 --> 00:09:14.000
You're the kind of artist
that can win "The Voice."

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:16.601
You can win this show.

00:09:16.601 --> 00:09:19.033
-Here we go. Here we go.
Get ready.

00:09:19.033 --> 00:09:22.767
John Legend, everybody.
"Legend" is out today.

00:09:22.767 --> 00:09:24.267
-Thank you.

00:09:24.267 --> 00:09:28.200
-And season 22 of "The Voice"
premieres September 19th on NBC.

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:30.267
We'll be right back with
Danielle Brooks, everybody.

00:09:30.267 --> 00:09:31.300
Stick around.

